  "knowledge": "Stellar Radius Value",
  "description": "Illustrates the value for a star's radius.",
  "definition": "Measured in solar radii ($R_{\\odot}$), where 1 is the radius of our Sun. Values range from small neutron stars to giant stars like Betelgeuse, which would extend beyond the orbit of Mars if in our solar system."
}

{
