  "knowledge": "Planet Radius Value",
  "description": "Illustrates the value for a planet's physical size.",
  "definition": "Typically measured in Jupiter radii ($R_J$). Earth's radius is about 0.09 $R_J$. Planets range from small rocky worlds smaller than Earth to 'inflated' gas giants larger than Jupiter."
}
